     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.4. Partnerships strengthened for innovative and inclusive South-South and triangular cooperation (Strategic Plan Output 1.1.1) 

The AI4COVID Project is to serve as a technical resource and knowledge networking hub for the COVID-19 Global South AI and Data Innovation Programme (COVID-AI programme) and facilitate knowledge synthesis as well as linkages to ensure timely flows of knowledge and expertise. 

PLJ is part of the UN Agencies involved in the ASEAN - UN Joint Strategic Plan of Action on Disaster Management (JSPADM) 2021-2025 to jointly mapping and coordinate UN projects aligning with the ADMERR (ASEAN Agreement on Disaster Management and Emergency Response) Work Plan. 

With UN Women and Indonesia&#x2019;s unicorn startup Gojek, PLJ conducted a mixed method research to look at how women micro entrepreneurs use digital platforms to start a business, generate revenue, or expand a business during the COVID-19 pandemic. The research was finalised and presented in early 2021 and has provided recommendations for UN Women, Gojek, and related Indonesian government agencies to support women micro entrepreneurs to cope with challenges during the pandemic and, where possible, grow their businesses. 

The initiative is followed by &#x201C;Beyond Sticky Floors, a design research piece focusing on support programs for women necessity business owners to utilize digital tools for their business as a way to cope with COVID-19 through an experimentation with behavioural economics principles to design behavioural change frameworks among these women.</narrative>
      </comment>
